      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-12-14_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <head>SAPPHIRE INSPIRATION.</head>
        <p>A SAPPHIRE INSPIRATION.</p>
        <p>The deep sea blue of the sapphire has inspired the idea of, many a beautiful gown, says a Globe writer. One of these, designed by herself, was worn by a beautiful Duchess at a great ball at which Royalty was present. The material was satin and chiffon, and the colour was just a tone paler than that of the immense sapphires them- selves. Lace was arranged upon the bodice in the novel way introduced this season, namely, caught into tasselled ends, each end 'fitted into a diamond pendant. The sleeves were arranged in exactly the same way. The sapphires them- selves consisted of a very high tiara, a very deep necklace, all set in superb brilliants, and ear- rings (now worn more dihan ever), and a few casual brooches, pinned here and there upon the lace of the bodice. A high collar (sixteen rows) encircled the fair neck, and had slides of bril- liants and sapphires. A rope of pearls completed the parure.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-12-14_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>FLOWERS IN JEWELS.</head>
        <p>FLOWERS IN JEWELS.</p>
        <p>Representations of flowers in the jewellery oi to-day are even more than usually popular. In rubies and diamonds, a spray for the hair repre- sents fuchsias with frosted leaves, the " frost " being merely clustered small diamonds on enamel. Another lovely ornament shows tose- buds in diamonds, a fully-blown rose in pink ones, and the stems in platinum.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-12-14_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>PRETTY EVENING BLOUSE.</head>
        <p>A PRETTY EVENING BLOUSE.</p>
        <p>Extremely dainty and becoming, as well as very original, is the charming blouse pictured in our sketch. Though so smart and dressy this blouse lends itself admirably to the making up of short lengths of material, and is really quite an economical design. Over the shoulders, fall- ing on to the sleeves, and pulled through the belt in front, is arranged a wide scarf of ivory lace, which lends all the style and this, to this pretty</p>
