        <p>CHICKEN EN CASSEROLE.--Cut, up a fowl into neat joints, and put into a stewpan one and a- lma ounce of butter or clarified dripping; let this melt, then put in the pieces of fowl with about a quir.rl:r of 1. pound of ham or badon (not . too fat) cut up small, a bunch of herbs, a slikd 1 carrot, two or three green onions, and a few pep- percorns, and fry it all together till the fowl is nicely browned, turning it once or twice and ; basting it. Pour off all superfluous fat, and put ; in half a gill of Marsala and one gill of good stock; cover the pap. and keep it simmering I gently in the oven, or at the side of the fire, from one and a half to two hours Then remove all the tat from the gravy, take out the herbs, and add another gill of stock, and, if liked, One tablespoonful more win. Serve in the casserole on a dish, with a napkin folded round. Rabbit limy be 000ked in exactly the same way.</p>
