      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-12-14_WidnesExaminer_art0150" n="art0150">
        <head>Warrington Outclass Swinton.</head>
        <p>Warrington Outclass Swinton.</p>
        <p>There was a crowd of 5,000 people to welcome the Swinton team to Wilderspool on Saturday. Heavy rain fell in the morning, but the afternoon conditions were pleasant, though the ground was somewhat heavy. Warrington had a strong team in the field, Fish reappearing after a long absence,while the visitors were also well represented. Teams : Warrington—Tilley, back ; Fish, Dickinson, Taylor, and Brooks, thredqaarter backs; Lees and Jenkins, half backs; Shngars, 'Thomas. A. E. Boardinan, Belton, Harmer, and Naylor, forwards. Swinton—Townson, back; Smith, Hoptvood, Valen- tine, and Griffin three-quarter backs ; Downing and Cunningham, laall backs; Simister (captain), Barnett, Taylor, Lloyd, Preston, and Davies, forwards. Referee—Mr. W. Robinson, Manningham : touch judges, Messrs. W. Crawshaw (Salford) and .1. Hassall (Broughton). Swinton were the first to become aggressive but Warrington eventually took up a strong attacking position, and Taylor cross-kicking to Fish, the latter raced over for a fine try, Thomas goaling from a difficult angle. Swinton rallied, only to be repulsed by Tilley, and Jenkins breaking away, passed to Thomas on the line, and scored. Jenkins was again to the fore with a bikliant run and serving Dickinson, the latter scored,Mrpoks adding the goal. Still maintaining the aggressive, Brooks scored after a fine round of passing. Swinton could not make any headway, and as the out- come of another fine bout of passing, initiated by Jenkins, Taylor scored, for Thomas to add the goal, whilst near the interval Townson mis-fielded, and let in Boardman, who placed the Swinton men further in arrears, Thomas adding his third goal. Half-time : Warrington, 4 goals 6 tries (26 points), Swinton nil. On changing ends it was expected that the rapid scoring would continue, but Swinton put up a better defence. Twice the home team looked certain scorers, when the Swinton men got offside and escaped with a penalty eel on each occasion from Thomas. Jenkins was again conspicuous with a clever run from the scrummage, and smart handling between him, Dickinson and eibh, resulted in the wing man racing in at the corner. Later on faylor got hurt in a tackle and left the field, Swinton holding their own baler after this. There was no more scoring, and the final came with the total : Warrington, 6 goals, 7 tries (33 points) ; Swinton, nil.</p>
      </div>
