        <head>MAYORAL "AT HOME."</head>
        <p>THE MAYORAL "AT HOME."</p>
        <p>SUCCESSFUL FUNCTION.</p>
        <p>The Mayor and Mayoress (Alderman and Mrs. Smethurst) held an "At Home" at the Town Hall on Thursday afternoon, and the function was a complete success. The large attendance testified to the universal respect in which the chief magistrate and his wife are held, there being a continuous stream of visitors from 3.30 to 5.30. The hall presented a very bright and aliimated appearance, decorations having been carried out in the best of taste. Flags and streamers embellished the exterior, the work having been entrusted to the borough Surveyor's depart- For Bronchial Coughs take Woods' Great Peppermint rnent, while in the vestibule of the hall Cure. 1/1, 2/9.—Advt. choice flowers and plants had been neatly arranged by Mr. R. Whitfield, the head gardener. On ; arrival the visitors were ushered into the Council ATKINSON &amp; BARKERS' Chamber where they were received by the Mayor and ROYAL Mayoress and the Misses Smethurst. The Mayoress • was elegantly .aowned in a rich black brocaded INFANT3' PRESERVATIVE. silk dress lrwith inner vest of old rose IN CONSTANT USE FOR OVER 100 YEARS. print lace over ivory chiffon together with outer vest FOR TEETHING, CONVULSIONS, RICKETS, ETC of hand made French lace, artistically embroidered Bottle; LA, 2/9 and 4/6. with helio chiffon roses and gold thread, the bodice being completed Ivith silver sequin and lace Bertha. The dress was supplied by the Misses Woods, ' Births. Rylands-street, Warrington. In the committee rooms FErtars—On December 10th, at Beecbgrove, Ashton-on- light refreshments were Ferved, the catering being in Ribble, Preston,the wife of Edwin Ferris, a daughter. the hands of Mr. Powys. A choice selection of music CultalE—On December 11th, at 119, Upper Brook- was given by Mr. A. Starkey's band, the programme street, the wife of W. E. Carrie, a dttughter. JoNEs—On the 7th inst., at Merchlyn, Couvvay,the wife being as follows : of (3. O. Jones, of a daughter. March "The Relief" A. Slfroni. Intermezzo-Valse " Salandre " George. Salonstruck " Stills Selansucht " %V. Aletter. Japanese Romance " Poppies ' Neil Moret. Selection "The Honeymooners" Geo. M. Cohan. ' The Regimental Patrol Theo. Ward. Graceful Dance " Vineta " ......W. Vandervell. Intermezzo Two-5tep...... " lola " L. Johnson. Three Deuces (a) " Gavotte " (b) "Eastern Dance" (c) 4' English Dance "...Cyril Scott. Poppourri "Die Meistersinger von Berlin" Paul Lincke. Valse-Reverie "Le Reve d'un Exil "Ch. Tourville. Overture "La Chevalier Breton "... A. Herman. Warrington.—Printed and published by JOHN WALREM Two-Step "Flying Arrow" A. Holzmann. &amp; Co., at The Examiner General Printing Works- Galop "The Motor Car" J. Gilchrist. Bewsey-street, and published by them at the same Valse " Undie Mans" Sydney House. , place, and also at The Examiner Offices, Victoria-road March "The Belle of Mayfair "...Leslie Stuart. Wins: 32, George-street, ST. 1:1111.XNs: 3, Market • treet, EARLBSToWN; Church-street RUNOOIIII Dec. For Children's Hacking Coughs at night, Woods Ilth, 1907, Great Peppermint Cure. 1/4 2/9.--Advt. •</p>
